{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#3266","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#3266","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#3266\",\"parent_revision\":\"d5144cd7a6ae4741f790045771e17982723b83a22efcbab9b82cd295375e7cc7\",\"root_revision\":\"d5144cd7a6ae4741f790045771e17982723b83a22efcbab9b82cd295375e7cc7\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P2\\ntype: Docs\\nstatus: open\\nadded: 2026-08-28\\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\n## Story\\n\\nAs a maintainer of the `work-backlog-item` skill, I want its runtime reference files to hold only what an executing agent needs to act, so that background philosophy and external research citations don't load into every consultation of that reference.\\n\\n## Description\\n\\n`plugins/development-harness/skills/work-backlog-item/references/workflows/work/sam-definition.md` opens with roughly 32 lines of \\\"What SAM Is\\\" and \\\"Core Principles\\\" background philosophy, and separately has a ~28-line \\\"Source\\\" section (lines ~48-76) containing external-repo pointers, git-clone instructions, and a dated \\\"Access date: 2026-02-23\\\" citation. Only a small middle portion of the file (roughly lines 34-44) is the actual operative definition an executing agent needs.\\n\\n## Impact\\n\\nThis file is loaded as a runtime reference during the `work-backlog-item` workflow. The philosophy and source-citation content don't change any action the executing agent takes \u2014 they're research provenance and conceptual framing, not instructions.\\n\\n## Observations\\n\\n- Flagged rather than fixed during a broader no-op/maintenance-note tightening pass, because trimming a ~60-line block spanning most of a short file needs a real look at what (if anything) is worth relocating to docs/, versus what can simply go \u2014 not a mechanical one-line trim.\\n\\n## Impact\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nThis file is loaded as a runtime reference during the `work-backlog-item` workflow. The philosophy and source-citation content don't change any action the executing agent takes \u2014 they're research provenance and conceptual framing, not instructions.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Story\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAs a maintainer of the `work-backlog-item` skill, I want its runtime reference files to hold only what an executing agent needs to act, so that background philosophy and external research citations don't load into every consultation of that reference.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Discovered during a no-op/maintenance-note sweep of development-harness skills and agents (2026-08-28)\\n- **Priority**: P2\\n- **Added**: 2026-08-28\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\\n## Observations\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- Flagged rather than fixed during a broader no-op/maintenance-note tightening pass, because trimming a ~60-line block spanning most of a short file needs a real look at what (if anything) is worth relocating to docs/, versus what can simply go \u2014 not a mechanical one-line trim.\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"c4b82ab4a00ed84d8a16b94b43506c083f1904b9bd202de76c333e94aa0922f7\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABRP6yhA\"}"}